---
import PolicyLayout from '~/layouts/PolicyLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/config/site';
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Editorial and Quality Policy"
  description="How Formatoza writes, tests and corrects its converter pages and guides: format-specific facts, tested claims, honest limitations and a clear corrections process."
  path="/editorial-policy/"
  h1="Editorial and quality policy"
  lead="Every page on Formatoza exists to help someone convert a file correctly. This policy describes how we keep that promise."
>
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Specific, not generic.</strong> Each converter page explains the actual formats
      involved — why they exist, where they break, what the conversion keeps and loses. We do not
      publish pages that differ only by format names.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Claims match behaviour.</strong> Statements about what a tool does — how it handles
      transparency, delimiters, multi-page files or malformed input — describe the tool's
      implemented behaviour, which is covered by automated tests with sample files.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Limitations are stated up front.</strong> Every converter lists what it cannot do. We
      don't claim “perfect” or “lossless” results where that isn't true.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A working tool on every page.</strong> We only publish a converter page when the
      converter works in current browsers.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How pages are produced</h2>
  <p>
    Content is drafted from a structured knowledge base of format facts, specifications (such as RFC
    4180 for CSV, RFC 4648 for Base64 and the W3C WebVTT specification) and our own testing. We use
    software tools, including AI writing assistants, to help draft and edit text; every page is then
    checked against the converter's real, tested behaviour before it is published.
  </p>
  <h2>Testing</h2>
  <p>
    Every conversion engine has automated tests covering valid files, empty and malformed input,
    large inputs, Unicode text, multiple files and file-name handling. Browser tests exercise each
    converter page end to end with real sample files.
  </p>
  <h2>Reviews and updates</h2>
  <p>
    Pages show the date they were last reviewed. We revisit pages when browser support changes (for
    example new AVIF or HEIC support), when libraries are updated, or when readers report problems.
  </p>
  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If something on the site is wrong or out of date, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. We correct factual errors
    promptly and update the review date.
  </p>
  <h2>Advertising and independence</h2>
  <p>
    Advertising funds the site but does not influence content. Ads are labelled, kept outside the
    converter, and never styled to look like download buttons. We do not accept payment for
    recommendations.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
